 ober Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade October Payme
 nt Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations\nAttention Trading Partners
 : MIHMS Upgrade October Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitation
 s\nAug 31\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Office of MaineCare 
 Services (OMS) is preparing to launch an upgraded version of MIHMS\, Maine
 Care’s claims processing system. The upgrade is currently scheduled to g
 o live on October 10\, 2026. To support a smooth transition\, OMS must imp
 lement temporary system access limitations and adjustments to payment cycl
 es in October.\nFrom Friday\, October 2 at 8:00 PM until Monday\, October 
 12 at 8:00 AM\, MIHMS will be in a “data freeze” while OMS completes f
 inal system readiness and transition activities.\nPlease note that we have
  updated the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of August 31\, 2026.\nChanges to
  October payment cycles:\nReview this information and plan billing accordi
 ngly to prepare for the transition.\nPayment Cycle Date\nPayment Impact\nC
 laim Submission Deadline for Inclusion in Payment Cycle*\nWednesday\, 9/30
 /26\nLast regular payment before the data freeze\nFriday\, 9/25/26\, 5:00 
 AM\nThursday\, 10/1/26\nExtra\npayment before the data freeze\nWednesday\,
  9/30/26\, 5:00 AM\nThere will be no payment on Wednesday\, October 7.\nTh
 ursday\, 10/15/26\nFirst payment after data freeze\, in upgraded system\nS
 ecure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) submission: Continuous through data fr
 eeze up to Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nPortal submission:\nBefore data f
 reeze: Friday\, 10/2/26\, 7:59 PM\nAfter data freeze: Tuesday\, 10/13/26\,
  2:00 PM\nWednesday\, 10/21/26\nRegular payment\, in upgraded system\nFrid
 ay\, 10/16/26\, 5:00 AM\n*\nAs always\, timely submission does not guarant
 ee that the claim will process in time for the next payment cycle. OMS may
  take up to 30 days to process and pay a claim\, depending on any edits or
  issues that may cause the clai\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/
 provider-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-paymen
 t-cycle-changes-and-system-access-0
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-cycle-changes-and-system-ac
 cess-0
