UID:ee66fea2fcec3af5@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Ovarian Cancer Awareness Month - September
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, ovarian cancer is the fifth leading cause of cance
 r deaths of women in the United States\, and it causes more deaths than an
 y other gynecologic cancer\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the American Cancer Society 
 estimates that 21\,010 cases of ovarian cancer will be newly diagnosed in 
 2026 and that 12\,450 individuals will die from the disease nationwide\, i
 ncluding 100 new cases and 70 deaths in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, many peop
 le are unaware of the symptoms of ovarian cancer\, which can often include
  bloating\, pelvic or abdominal pain\, difficulty eating or feeling full q
 uickly\, urinary issues\, and several more that are easily confused with o
 ther diseases\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, the lack of an early detection test for o
 varian cancer combined with its vague symptoms means that approximately 80
  percent of cases of ovarian cancer are detected at an advanced stage\; an
 d\nWHEREAS\n\, all women are at risk for ovarian cancer\, but approximatel
 y 20 percent of women who are diagnosed with ovarian cancer have a heredit
 ary predisposition to the disease which places them at even higher risk\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, the family history of a woman has been found to play an i
 mportant role in accurately assessing their risk of developing ovarian can
 cer\, and medical experts believe that family history should be taken into
  consideration during the annual well-woman visit of any woman\; and\nWHER
 EAS\n\, ongoing investments in ovarian cancer research and education and a
 wareness efforts are critical to closing these gaps and improving survivor
 ship for women with ovarian cancer\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved tha
 t I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim
  September 2026 as\nOvarian Cancer Awareness Month\nthroughout the State o
 f Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testim
 ony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto a
 ffixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this twenty seventh\nof August Two 
 Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_document
 s/proclamations/2026-08-ovarian-cancer-awareness-month-september
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-ovarian-cancer-awareness-month-september
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c53cca3e4173a844@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260828T221633Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] GEAR UP Week - September 21 through 25
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Gaining Early Awareness and Readiness for Undergra
 duate Programs (GEAR UP) is a federal grant program designed to increase t
 he number of low-income students who are prepared to enter and succeed in 
 postsecondary education and careers\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, GEAR UP Maine was f
 ounded in 1998\, and since then has helped prepare over 29\,000 students t
 o pursue education and career pathways they otherwise may not have been ab
 le to\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, administered by the University of Maine Farmingto
 n and the nonprofit Syntiro\, GEAR UP Maine supports students beginning in
  7th grade through high school and onward as they prepare for college\, ca
 reers\, and lifelong success\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, support provided by GEAR U
 P includes tutoring\, mentoring\, financial education\, college scholarshi
 ps\, career exploration\, and more\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, GEAR UP Maine will s
 erve 5\,000 students in seventh through twelfth grade during the current g
 rant period of 2023-2030\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine is committed to providin
 g a high-quality education for all students and helping them reach their h
 ighest potential\, no matter the path they choose\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, b
 e it resolved that I\, Janet Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do h
 ereby proclaim the week of September 21-25\, 2026 as\nGEAR UP Week\nthroug
 hout the State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this observ
 ance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State t
 o be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this twenty seventh
  day\nof August Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mil
 ls/official_documents/proclamations/2026-08-gear-week-september-21-through
 -25
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-gear-week-september-21-through-25
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
